# JavaScript Basics Cheat Sheet

## Variables
```javascript
let age = 20;        // Can be changed
const PI = 3.14;     // Cannot be changed
var name = "John";   // Old way
```

## Data Types
```javascript
Number
String
Boolean
Null
Undefined
Object
Array
```

## Operators

### Arithmetic
```javascript
+  -  *  /  %  **
```

### Comparison
```javascript
==  ===  !=  !==  >  <  >=  <=
```

### Logical
```javascript
&&  ||  !
```

## Input & Output
```javascript
alert("Hello");
prompt("Enter your name");
console.log("Hello");
```

## if Statement
```javascript
if (age >= 18) {
    console.log("Adult");
}
```

## if...else
```javascript
if (age >= 18) {
    console.log("Adult");
} else {
    console.log("Minor");
}
```

## switch
```javascript
switch(day) {
    case 1:
        console.log("Monday");
        break;
    default:
        console.log("Invalid");
}
```

## for Loop
```javascript
for (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    console.log(i);
}
```

## while Loop
```javascript
let i = 1;
while (i <= 5) {
    console.log(i);
    i++;
}
```

## Function
```javascript
function add(a, b) {
    return a + b;
}
```

## Arrow Function
```javascript
const add = (a, b) => a + b;
```

## Arrays
```javascript
let fruits = ["Apple", "Mango", "Orange"];

fruits.push("Banana");
fruits.pop();
fruits.shift();
fruits.unshift("Grapes");
```

## Strings
```javascript
let text = "JavaScript";

text.length;
text.toUpperCase();
text.toLowerCase();
text.slice(0, 4);
text.includes("Java");
```

## Objects
```javascript
let student = {
    name: "Rakesh",
    age: 20
};

console.log(student.name);
```

## DOM
```javascript
document.getElementById("id");
document.querySelector(".class");
document.querySelectorAll("p");
```

## Change Content
```javascript
element.innerText = "Hello";
element.innerHTML = "<b>Hello</b>";
```

## Change CSS
```javascript
element.style.color = "red";
```

## Events
```javascript
button.addEventListener("click", () => {
    alert("Button Clicked");
});
```

## Template Literals
```javascript
let name = "Rakesh";
console.log(`Hello ${name}`);
```

